§ `Kinnim chapter 1`

§§ `1:1 above and below`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:2 | חטאת העוף נעשית למטה, וחטאת בהמה למעלה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:3 | עולת העוף נעשית למעלה, ועולת הבהמה למטה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:4 | אם שינה בזה ובזה, פסול.
-- A bird's sin offering is made below [the red line], a beast's sin offering above.
-- A bird's burnt offering is made above, a beast's burnt offering below.
-- If he changed it in either, it is invalid.
@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:2-4)
GIVEN animal   IS AN `Animal`
      offering IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH A `Level`
`the level prescribed for` animal offering MEANS
    CONSIDER animal
    WHEN bird THEN
        CONSIDER offering
        WHEN `sin offering`  THEN below
        WHEN `burnt offering` THEN above
    WHEN beast THEN
        CONSIDER offering
        WHEN `sin offering`  THEN above
        WHEN `burnt offering` THEN below

@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:4)
GIVEN animal   IS AN `Animal`
      offering IS AN `Offering`
      level    IS A `Level`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an offering made at this level is valid` animal offering level MEANS
    level EQUALS `the level prescribed for` animal offering

§§ `1:1 what a pair is offered as`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:5 | סדר קנים כך הוא:
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:6 | החובה, אחד חטאת ואחד עולה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:7 | בנדרים ונדבות, כולן עולות.
-- The order of nests is this: the obligation, one sin offering and one burnt offering; in vows and
-- gifts, all are burnt offerings.
@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:5-7)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of the offering`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sin offerings in a pair brought as` ground MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN obligation THEN 1
    WHEN vow        THEN 0
    WHEN gift       THEN 0

@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:6-7)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of the offering`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`burnt offerings in a pair brought as` ground MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN obligation THEN 1
    WHEN vow        THEN 2
    WHEN gift       THEN 2

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:8 | איזהו נדר, האומר הרי עלי עולה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:9 | ואיזהו נדבה, האומר הרי זו עולה.
-- What is a vow?  One who says "I take a burnt offering upon me".  And what is a gift?  One who says
-- "this one is a burnt offering".
@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:8-9)
GIVEN words IS A `Words of dedication`
GIVETH A `Ground of the offering`
`what words of dedication make the offering` words MEANS
    CONSIDER words
    WHEN `it is upon me` THEN vow
    WHEN `this one is`   THEN gift

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:10 | מה בין נדרים לנדבות, אלא שהנדרים, מתו או נגנבו, חייבים באחריותם.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:11 | ונדבות, מתו או נגנבו, אין חייבים באחריותן.
-- What is between vows and gifts?  Only that for vows, if they died or were stolen, one is answerable
-- for them; and for gifts, if they died or were stolen, one is not answerable for them.
-- The text speaks of vows and gifts only, so an obligation answers NOTHING here.
@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:10-11)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of the offering`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the owner must replace it if it died or was stolen` ground MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN vow        THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN gift       THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN obligation THEN NOTHING

§§ `1:2 to 1:3 how many birds of a mixture may be offered, when the priest asks first`

-- The rule of chapters 1 and 2 is that the priest who asks is told to offer only what is valid in
-- EVERY way the birds could have been (Bartenura on 1:2 and 1:3).  A mixture is never settled by
-- its majority: living creatures are not nullified (Bartenura on 1:2, "בעלי חיים חשיבי ולא בטלי").
-- So the first rule below is the definition, stated for every possible world, and the second is the
-- count it gives; kn-tests.l4 checks that they agree.

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:13 | חטאת שנתערבה בעולה, ועולה בחטאת, אפילו אחד בריבוא, ימותו כולם.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:14 | חטאת שנתערבה בחובה, אין כשר אלא כמנין חטאות שבחובה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:15 | וכן עולה שנתערבה בחובה, אין כשר אלא כמנין עולות שבחובה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:16 | בין שהחובה מרובה והנדבה מועטת, בין שהנדבה מרובה והחובה מועטת, בין ששתיהן שוות.
-- A sin offering that was mixed with a burnt offering, or a burnt offering with a sin offering, even
-- one in ten thousand: all of them die.  A sin offering that was mixed with an obligation: only as many
-- as the sin offerings in the obligation are valid.  So too a burnt offering mixed with an obligation:
-- only as many as the burnt offerings in the obligation.  Whether the obligation is many and the gift
-- few, or the gift many and the obligation few, or both are equal.
@ref Kinnim 1:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:13-16)
GIVEN m    IS A `Mixture`
      kind IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`designated birds of the other kind in the mixture` m kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sin offering`   THEN m's `designated burnt offerings`
    WHEN `burnt offering` THEN m's `designated sin offerings`

@ref Kinnim 1:2 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:14-15)
GIVEN o    IS AN `Unassigned obligation`
      kind IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`offerings of this kind owed by the obligation` o kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sin offering`   THEN o's `sin offerings owed`
    WHEN `burnt offering` THEN o's `burnt offerings owed`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:19 | אבל בחובה שנתערבה זו בזו, אחת לזו ואחת לזו, שתים לזו ושתים לזו, שלש לזו ושלש לזו, מחצה כשר ומחצה פסול.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:20 | אחת לזו ושתים לזו, ושלש לזו, ועשר לזו, ומאה לזו, המועט כשר, בין משם אחד, בין משני שמות, בין מאשה אחת, בין משתי נשים.
-- But an obligation mixed with another: one to this woman and one to that, two and two, three and
-- three: half are valid and half invalid.  One to this and two to that, and three to that, and ten to
-- that, and a hundred to that: the fewest is valid; whether for one reason or for two reasons, whether
-- of one woman or of two women.
-- THE DEFINITION.  If the priest offers k birds of one kind out of the mixture, every one of them is
-- valid in every possible world exactly when: no designated bird of the other kind is in the mixture
-- (any of the k could be it), and no unassigned obligation owes fewer than k of that kind (all k could
-- have been hers).  With no unassigned obligation, the k must come from designated birds of the kind.
@ref Kinnim 1:2-1:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:13-16 src:mishnah-kinnim-1:19-20)
GIVEN m    IS A `Mixture`
      kind IS AN `Offering`
      k    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` m kind k MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF k EQUALS 0
            THEN TRUE
        IF `designated birds of the other kind in the mixture` m kind GREATER THAN 0
            THEN FALSE
        IF null (m's `unassigned obligations`)
            THEN k AT MOST (`designated birds of the other kind in the mixture` m (`the other offering` kind))
        OTHERWISE
            all (GIVEN o YIELD k AT MOST (`offerings of this kind owed by the obligation` o kind)) (m's `unassigned obligations`)

@ref Kinnim 1:1 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:6)
GIVEN kind IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH AN `Offering`
`the other offering` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `sin offering`   THEN `burnt offering`
    WHEN `burnt offering` THEN `sin offering`

-- THE COUNT the definition gives: the largest such k.  "The fewest is valid" (המועט כשר): the
-- smallest number any one obligation owes of that kind.
@ref Kinnim 1:2-1:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:13-16 src:mishnah-kinnim-1:19-20)
GIVEN m    IS A `Mixture`
      kind IS AN `Offering`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` m kind MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `designated birds of the other kind in the mixture` m kind GREATER THAN 0
            THEN 0
        IF null (m's `unassigned obligations`)
            THEN `designated birds of the other kind in the mixture` m (`the other offering` kind)
        OTHERWISE
            minimum (map (GIVEN o YIELD `offerings of this kind owed by the obligation` o kind) (m's `unassigned obligations`))

-- The birds of the mixture that may be offered, both kinds together; the rest must die.
@ref Kinnim 1:2-1:3 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:13-16 src:mishnah-kinnim-1:19-20)
GIVEN m IS A `Mixture`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the birds of the mixture that may be offered` m MEANS
        `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` m `sin offering`
    PLUS `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` m `burnt offering`

GIVEN m IS A `Mixture`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the birds in the mixture` m MEANS
        m's `designated sin offerings`
    PLUS m's `designated burnt offerings`
    PLUS sum (map (GIVEN o YIELD o's `sin offerings owed` PLUS o's `burnt offerings owed`) (m's `unassigned obligations`))

-- A whole unassigned nest of p pairs.
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unassigned obligation`
`a nest of pairs` p MEANS
    `Unassigned obligation` WITH
        `sin offerings owed`   IS p
        `burnt offerings owed` IS p

-- Whole nests of the given numbers of pairs, mixed with nothing designated (1:3).
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Mixture`
`nests mixed together` counts MEANS
    `Mixture` WITH
        `designated sin offerings`   IS 0
        `designated burnt offerings` IS 0
        `unassigned obligations`     IS map `a nest of pairs` counts

§§ `1:4 one reason or two; Rabbi Yose`

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:22 | כיצד משם אחד, לידה ולידה, זיבה וזיבה, משם אחד.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:23 | משני שמות, לידה וזיבה.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:24 | כיצד שתי נשים, על זו לידה ועל זו לידה, על זו זיבה ועל זו זיבה, משם אחד.
-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:25 | משני שמות, על זו לידה ועל זו זיבה.
-- How "of one reason"?  Childbirth and childbirth, discharge and discharge: of one reason.  Of two
-- reasons: childbirth and discharge.  How "of two women"?  For this one childbirth and for that one
-- childbirth, for this one discharge and for that one discharge: of one reason.  Of two reasons: for
-- this one childbirth and for that one discharge.
-- The rule of 1:3 takes neither the reason nor the owner as an input: that is what "whether for one
-- reason or for two, of one woman or of two" says.  This rule only names the distinction.
@ref Kinnim 1:4 (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:22-25)
GIVEN first  IS A `Reason for the obligation`
      second IS A `Reason for the obligation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two obligations are of one reason` first second MEANS
    first EQUALS second

-- src:mishnah-kinnim-1:26 | רבי יוסי אומר, שתי נשים שלקחו קניהן בערוב, או שנתנו דמי קניהן לכהן, לאיזו שירצה כהן יקריב חטאת, ולאיזו שירצה כהן יקריב עולה, בין משם אחד, בין משני שמות.
-- Rabbi Yose says: two women who bought their nests jointly, or who gave the price of their nests to
-- the priest: for whichever he wishes the priest offers a sin offering, and for whichever he wishes a
-- burnt offering, whether of one reason or of two.
-- Bartenura: the halakha follows Rabbi Yose, and he speaks of women who agreed to this when they
-- bought (Eruvin 36b).  Nothing of theirs is then lost to the mixing: the priest assigns each bird.
@ref Kinnim 1:4, Rabbi Yose (src:mishnah-kinnim-1:26)
GIVEN `bought their nests jointly`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave the price of their nests to the priest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the priest may assign each bird to whichever woman he wishes` `bought their nests jointly` `gave the price of their nests to the priest` MEANS
    `bought their nests jointly` OR `gave the price of their nests to the priest`
